  "season": null,
  "sourceType": "SYNTHESISED",
  "sourceNotes": "Pilau (also spelled pilaf, pulao) is one of the most widespread rice preparations in the world, found from Iran to India to Central Asia. The British curry-house version uses basmati rice with cardamom, cloves, and cinnamon, often coloured golden with turmeric or saffron. It has been a standard accompaniment to British curry since the 1960s. Madhur Jaffrey, Madhur Jaffrey's Indian Cookery (BBC Books, 1982) covers the absorption method.",
