  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pilau rice is basmati cooked by the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "absorption method",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "absorption-method"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with whole spices and onion. The spices toast in butter before the rice goes in, which perfumes the fat and carries the fragrance into every grain. The finished rice is golden, with long separate grains. Rinsing the rice before cooking is the step that prevents stickiness."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
